\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Simulated correlations between the polar scattering angles ($\theta _1$,$\theta _2$) of two protons undergoing elastic scattering, shown for beam energies of 10, 100, 300, 500, 700, 900, and 1000 MeV. The uppermost straight line corresponds to a beam energy of 10 MeV, where the opening angle between the two protons is approximately $90^{\circ }$, as expected in the non-relativistic regime. As the beam energy increases, relativistic effects cause a pronounced bending of the correlation curves, particularly in the region of symmetric polar angles. These effects become increasingly significant with higher beam energies. Courtesy: \textit  {Mrunmoy Jena}.\relax }}{28}{figure.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
